    Explain with more treatment to the basic use case

    It being named "basic" doesn't make it any less
    legitimate of a use case than the primitive index
    form with explicit bounds!  In fact I have grown
    to quite like this form myself; and at least to me,
    letting you address array elements with a short name
    independently of your naming choice on the array
    itself is pretty nice... :]

    Either way, just documenting it helps in general
    too.  I bet people will inevitably wince at the
    *_ = $img binding accompanied by $ok->($mid) and
    wonder why the same thing appears to be uselessly
    repeated (it's not *that* useful (not to me for
    the time being at least), but I hate to throw away
    information that cannot be trivially recovered...).

